SUMMARY:Stony Knob to Elk Pasture
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nNOTE THE CHANGE\n\nwatching the we
 ather 👀\n\napprox 7 mile 1200 ft out and back on the MST/Shut In. three
  overlooks: Stony Bald\, Big Ridge\, Mills River\, then on to Elk Pasture 
 (turnaround point)\n\nanticipated pace 2.5 ish mph\n\nwell-behaved dogs ar
 e welcome!\n\nper previous hikes:\n\ngear up as appropriate\, trekking pol
 es are an option. bring a snack as we'll take a break mid-hike. and plenty
  of water\n\nground rules: 1) if you sign up\, show up or change your stat
 us. 2 ) be sure you are in adequate physical shape to complete the event. 
 3) show consideration toward all attendees. I hike for stress reduction an
 d want to keep it that way as much as possible\n\nLEGALESE\nThis Asheville
  Hiking Group event involves hiking and\, possibly\, transportation to and
  from the meetup site. Participants are responsible for their own safety a
 nd affirm that they have the appropriate skills\, physical conditioning\, 
 equipment\, and supplies. Hiking may involve risks to oneself and property
 . Neither your hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group can assure your s
 afety nor eliminate all risks. By signing up for this event\, participant 
 understands and agrees
